Hi Jiri,

A few comments on this patch inline.

> From 7966dfb03cf6faa2cb02fbf7b1c270e3f11b230b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
> From: Jiri Pirko <jiri@nvidia.com>
> Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:50:39 +0200
> Subject: [PATCH 06/20] ctlv: Prepare blob descriptor validation
>
> Add parsing and VA checks for blob descriptors shared by schema
> validation and runtime acquisition.
>
> Keep CONFIG_CTLV unwired until dispatch completes the module.

The "unwired" approach means nothing in `drivers/ctlv` is compiled until a later patch adds the hook-up, so this patch (and the Makefile hunk) gets zero build coverage, and any compile error here would only show up many patches later and be blamed on the wrong commit. Please either wire `CONFIG_CTLV` (even with a stub) early, or at least state in the commit message that this was build-tested out of tree.

Also the commit message is thin: "VA checks" is misleading. The only checks are non-zero length, `max_len`, alignment and start+length overflow. Nothing verifies the address is a user address (no `access_ok()`/`TASK_SIZE` style bound), which a reader would expect from "VA checks"; please say where that happens.

