Summary of the most serious issues for patch 6:
 - Nothing in this patch is compiled (`CONFIG_CTLV` unwired), so zero bisect/build coverage.
 - Dead code / speculative generality: FD and OFFSET members, the OFFSET start selection, one-case switch in `ctlv_blob_variant()`.
 - `IS_ALIGNED()` with alignment 0 or non-power-of-two; BIT(type) shift hazard once more types exist; write-only `end`.
 - "VA checks" in the commit message overstates: no user-address bound is checked.
 - Inconsistent flag policy versus `schema.c` (`IGNORE_IF_UNKNOWN`), unreasoned `u64` reads, no kernel-doc.
